The Javascript Math object provides a collection of properties and methods for mathematical constants and functions.

A. Basic Math Methods

1. Math.abs(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the absolute value of a number
Example:
Math.abs(-5); // returns 5
Math.abs(3.14); // returns 3.14

2. Math.ceil(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Rounds a number up to the nearest integer
Example:
Math.ceil(4.2); // returns 5
Math.ceil(-2.7); // returns -2

3. Math.floor(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Rounds a number down to the nearest integer
Example:
Math.floor(4.9); // returns 4
Math.floor(-2.7); // returns -3

4. Math.round(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Rounds a number to the nearest integer
Example:
Math.round(4.4); // returns 4
Math.round(4.5); // returns 5
Math.round(-1.6); // returns -2

5. Math.max([x[, y[, ...]]])
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the largest of zero or more numbers
Example:
Math.max(10, 20, 30); // returns 30
Math.max(-1, -2, -3); // returns -1

6. Math.min([x[, y[, ...]]])
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the smallest of zero or more numbers
Example:
Math.min(10, 20, 30); // returns 10
Math.min(-1, -2, -3); // returns -3

7. Math.trunc(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the integer part of a number by removing any fractional digits
Example:
Math.trunc(4.9); // returns 4
Math.trunc(-2.7); // returns -2

8. Math.pow(x, y)
Return type: Number
Description: Returns x raised to the power of y
Example:
Math.pow(2, 3); // returns 8
Math.pow(4, 0.5); // returns 2

9. Math.random()
Return type: Number
Description: Returns a pseudo-random number between 0 (inclusive) and 1 (exclusive)
Example:
Math.random(); // returns a random number like 0.123456789
// To get a random number between min and max:
function getRandom(min, max) {
  return Math.random() * (max - min) + min;
}

10. Math.sqrt(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the square root of a number
Example:
Math.sqrt(9); // returns 3
Math.sqrt(2); // returns ~1.4142

11. Math.cbrt(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the cube root of a number
Example:
Math.cbrt(8); // returns 2
Math.cbrt(-27); // returns -3

12. Math.hypot([x[, y[, ...]]])
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the square root of the sum of squares of its arguments
Example:
Math.hypot(3, 4); // returns 5
Math.hypot(1, 1, 1, 1); // returns 2

13. Math.sign(x)
Return type: Number
Description: Returns the sign of a number (1, -1, 0, -0, or NaN)
Example:
Math.sign(5); // returns 1
Math.sign(-5); // returns -1
Math.sign(0); // returns 0